# Draft: d2d1 Implement ID2D1SvgDocument and ID2D1SvgElement DOM methods
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12802 state=opened
# As a draft, I'm mainly looking for direction on the questions below before going further, rather than full review.

[Bug 57564](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=57564) is caused by the stubbed CreateSvgDocument and DrawSvgDocument within d2d1.  This series represents the first part of implementing those.

What the series contains:
- `ID2D1SvgDocument` and `ID2D1SvgElement` IDL, creating document and root, creating/removing/inserting/replacing elements, text content, walking the element tree.
- Reference counting matches Windows: holding a reference to an element keeps its ancestors and the document alive.
- vtable order for `ID2D1SvgElement` was determined on Windows by calling each slot of a native SvgElement and identifying the method from its behavior (return values and effect on the tree).
- Which elements may contain which is tested and matches Windows.

Not in this series: attributes, XML loading, drawing.

Open Questions/Confirmations:
- `SetAttributeValue` and `GetAttributeValue` each have three distinct entries in the vtable.  To handle this overloading, I've used suffixes such as `_String`, `_Attribute`, `_POD`, and `_IID`. Is this acceptable, or is there a preferable way to handle this, or better naming? Note that mingw-w64's header orders slots 27–33 differently, but the order here was verified by probing on Windows.
- For XML parsing, does xmllite's IXmlReader (which is already used in D2D) seem like the way to go?
- Preliminary testing of attributes has shown that they are validated and parsed when set (setting `1in` and reading it back returns `96`), and enumerated in alphabetical order by attribute name.  I anticipate storing them in a sorted per-element array of {attribute id, value}, with attribute id coming from an enum, and value being a union of float/string/D2D types. Does that approach work for you?
